  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>When phenol reacts with chloroform in the presence of bases (NaOH/KOH), an aldehyde (&minus;CHO) group gets introduced in the ring at a position ortho to the phenolic group and salicylaldehyde is formed. This reaction is called the Reimer-Tiemann reaction. Reaction occurs according to the following mechanism.&nbsp;&nbsp;<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/a6ebc3f5-9fc4-49cb-9103-b994eb50ccbe-image.png\" style=\"width: 550px; height: 295px;\" /></p><p>So, intermediate formed will be</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/e222f6f3-bee8-4861-a54b-847e8dc4656a-image.png\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 153px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
